※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4562 LANG_BORROW_SAYS_NOTHING
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4561 LANG_BORROW_NOT_FROM_IT

※ A lifetime name is on the reference it is written on.  `& &⧖a u32` names a
※ place holding a reference that lives as long as `⧖a`, and says nothing of how
※ long that place is there; and where it does say, `&v` is the place `v` is
※ kept in this call, not what `v` named.

fn slot(v: &⧖a u32) → & &⧖a u32:
    &v

fn kept(v: &⧖a u32) → &⧖a &⧖a u32:
    &v

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup, impure]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let x: u32 = 1u32
    if kept(&x)⌖⌖ = 1u32: 0u6 else: 1u6
